  "source": {
    "harness": "code/run_midterm_sweep.py with code/minimal_full_server.py and code/openai_engine_adapter.py; validated by code/export_midterm_results.py. Baseline and vLLM ran in WSL2 Ubuntu (Python 3.12, vllm==0.8.5.post1, torch 2.6.0+cu124). llama.cpp used the official Windows CUDA 12.4 llama-server b11765 against TheBloke TinyLlama Q8_0 GGUF. vLLM: `vllm serve TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0 --dtype half --max-model-len 2048 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.75`. llama.cpp: `llama-server -m tinyllama-1.1b-chat-v1.0.Q8_0.gguf -ngl 99 -c 8192 --parallel 4` (8192 is a shared KV pool so 4 clients each keep a 2048-token slot).",
    "json_file": "report/src/data/srk2211-midterm-results.json",
    "started": "2026-10-20T21:55:30-04:00",
    "finished": "2026-10-20T22:05:16-04:00",
    "workload": {
      "prompt_token_targets": [
        128,
        512,
        1920
      ],
      "max_new_tokens": 64,
      "concurrency_grid": [
        1,
        4
      ],
      "reps_per_cell": 3,
      "warmup_runs": 1,
      "notes": "Synthetic TCP/networking prompts from code/workload/prompts.json, sized with TinyLlama chat template (add_generation_prompt=true). The long cell is labeled syn_2048 but capped at 1920 templated tokens so prompt + 64 decode fits TinyLlama's 2048-token context. HF engines (baseline, vLLM) measured 128 / 512 / 1920 tokens. llama.cpp counted 131 / 522 / 1956 on the same texts. WildChat train indices 42 and 2048 were generated for sanity checks but are not part of the 18-row matrix. KV bytes are the dense FP16 GQA formula from HW1 (2 * 2B * 22 layers * 4 KV heads * seq_len * 64). llama.cpp used Q8_0 GGUF; that quantization is a confounder versus the FP16 Hugging Face weights used by baseline and vLLM. llama.cpp long-prompt TTFT stayed ~34-60 ms after a same-prompt warmup, consistent with prefix reuse in addition to the C++ runtime."
    }
  },
  "systems": [
    {
      "id": "minimal_b1",
      "label": "minimal_full_server (batch=1)",
      "family": "baseline",
      "description": "Week 2 five-step server instrumented in code/minimal_full_server.py: one worker, FIFO queue, contiguous Hugging Face DynamicCache, no iteration-level batching. Concurrent clients start together; queue wait is included in TTFT.",
      "novelty": "Contiguous DynamicCache and no iteration-level batching — N>1 TTFT becomes a staircase because later clients wait for each earlier request's full prefill + decode."
    },
    {
      "id": "vllm_paged",
      "label": "vLLM PagedAttention",
      "family": "vllm",
      "description": "vllm 0.8.5.post1 serving TinyLlama FP16 over the OpenAI-compatible HTTP API. Concurrent streaming clients from code/openai_engine_adapter.py.",
      "novelty": "PagedAttention plus continuous batching: at N=4, decode TBT stays near the N=1 value while TTFT rises from shared prefill, not from serializing whole requests.",
      "repo": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm"
    },
    {
      "id": "llama_cpp",
      "label": "llama.cpp llama-server (Q8_0)",
      "family": "llama.cpp",
      "description": "Official Windows CUDA 12.4 llama-server b11765, TinyLlama 1.1B Chat Q8_0 GGUF, 4 parallel slots, 8192-token shared context pool. Same OpenAI-compatible streaming client as vLLM.",
      "novelty": "C++/GGUF runtime with slot-based continuous batching; KV is preallocated per slot. Q8_0 quantization and possible prefix reuse after warmup both affect the numbers and are disclosed.",
      "repo": "https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp"
    }
  ],
