  "takeaways": [
    "At concurrency 1, 512-token TTFT is 449 ms (baseline), 412 ms (vLLM), and 40 ms (llama.cpp Q8). TBT p50 is 51.1 / 35.6 / 22.2 ms. llama.cpp's gap includes Q8 quantization, not only scheduling.",
    "The baseline novelty is queueing, not decode speed: at N=4 and 512 tokens, median TTFT jumps from 449 ms to 6280 ms and the slowest client hits 12044 ms, while per-token TBT stays ~50 ms. Four clients share one worker, so TTFT is a staircase.",
    "vLLM continuous batching cuts that tail: N=4 512-token median TTFT is 1562 ms (max sample 1638 ms) versus the baseline's 6280 / 12044 ms. TBT stays near the single-user value because decode iterations are shared.",
    "llama.cpp slot batching keeps N=4 512-token TTFT at 72 ms (max sample 79 ms). Long-prompt N=1 TTFT is 34 ms after warmup versus 1627 / 1393 ms for the FP16 engines — treat that as Q8 + possible prefix reuse, not a pure scheduler win.",
    "Dense KV bytes scale linearly with seq_len and match across the two FP16 engines (4.3 / 13.0 / 44.7 MB at 192 / 576 / 1984 tokens). llama.cpp is a few percent higher only because its tokenizer counted a few extra prompt tokens on the same text."
  ],
  "summary": "On an RTX 4060 Laptop (8 GB) with TinyLlama 1.1B, the Week 2 minimal server, vLLM 0.8.5, and llama.cpp Q8 were compared on the same 128 / 512 / 1920-token prompts at concurrency 1 and 4 (3 reps after 1 warmup). Baseline TTFT explodes at N=4 because it finishes one full request before starting the next (6280 ms median at 512 tokens, 12044 ms worst client). vLLM's continuous batching and PagedAttention keep the same N=4 cell at 1562 ms median / 1638 ms max while TBT stays near the N=1 line. llama.cpp is the fastest wall-clock engine (72 ms median TTFT at the same cell), but it ran a Q8 GGUF after a same-prompt warmup, so that comparison is not FP16-apples-to-apples. KV bytes follow the dense GQA formula on every engine.",
  "plot": {
    "title": "Median TTFT vs prompt length (concurrency = 1)",
    "metric": "ttft_ms",
    "x_field": "prompt_tokens",
    "series_field": "system_id",
    "aggregate": "median",
    "filter": {
      "concurrency": 1
    },
    "y_label": "TTFT (ms)",
    "x_label": "Prompt tokens"
  },
  "boxplot": {
